---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { graph, counts } from '../lib/data.ts';

const c = counts();
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="About SAICA-KG — a faceted knowledge graph of supervision tools for AI coding agents."
>
  <h1>About SAICA-KG</h1>
  <p class="mt-3 text-lg text-ink-muted max-w-3xl">
    A faceted knowledge graph of supervision tools for AI coding agents.
  </p>

  <section class="mt-8 max-w-3xl leading-7">
    <p>
      SAICA-KG classifies supervision tools along three orthogonal strict partitions —
      <strong>ControlParadigm</strong> (prevention / detection / correction / recovery),
      <strong>TemporalPhase</strong> (pre_generation / in_generation / post_generation),
      and <strong>AutonomyLevel</strong> (fully_autonomous / graduated_hitl / full_hitl) —
      plus multi-valued <strong>FailureMode</strong> tags.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4">
      It absorbs existing failure-mode taxonomies (OWASP Agentic Top 10, MAST, DAPLab
      9 Patterns, Microsoft AIRT) as first-class data with explicit crosswalks into our
      facets. Queries like <em>"which supervisors cover OWASP ASI04 at post-generation
      in graduated-HITL?"</em> resolve against the graph with explicit citations.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4">
      <strong>Navigational, not evaluative.</strong> SAICA-KG returns ranked sets with
      explicit criteria, not endorsed winners.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-10 max-w-3xl leading-7">
    <h2>Design principle: honest MECE</h2>
    <p class="mt-2">
      The partitions are strict — every Tool fits exactly one cell on each of
      ControlParadigm, TemporalPhase, and AutonomyLevel. Tools that legitimately
      span cells are <em>split</em> into multiple Tool nodes rather than dual-tagged,
      so facet counts stay truthful. MECE cells with no tools are visible as gaps
      rather than silently hidden — the coverage report flags under-filled cells
      instead of papering over them. Multi-valued tags (FailureMode, LocusOfControl)
      live alongside the strict partitions for the many-to-many relations that
      don't fit a clean taxonomy. See
      <a href="https://github.com/saica-kg/saica-kg/blob/main/EDITORIAL_POLICY.md" rel="noopener">EDITORIAL_POLICY.md</a>
      for the full inclusion criteria and RFC process.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-10 max-w-3xl leading-7">
    <h2>Five ways to consume the KG</h2>
    <ol class="mt-2 list-decimal pl-6 space-y-2">
      <li>
        <strong>Browse</strong> — this website renders one page per node with
        facet-filtered search at <a href="/tools">/tools</a>,
        <a href="/failure-modes">/failure-modes</a>, <a href="/taxonomies">/taxonomies</a>,
        <a href="/papers">/papers</a>, plus an interactive Cytoscape graph at
        <a href="/graph">/graph</a>.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>JSON API</strong> — machine-readable endpoints at
        <a href="/api/v1/snapshot.json"><code>/api/v1/snapshot.json</code></a> and
        per-collection / per-node JSON. Fetched over standard HTTP, no auth.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>GitHub YAML</strong> — clone the repo and read
        <code>data/**/*.yml</code> directly. One file per node, CC-BY-4.0.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Ingestion pipeline</strong> — the <code>pipeline/</code> tree drives
        automated discovery (Perplexity / Elicit / Semantic Scholar / GitHub /
        awesome-lists), Postgres staging, NLP preprocess, Cohere Rerank semantic
        filtering, and Azure Kimi-K2.5 structured extraction. See
        <a href="/pipeline">/pipeline</a> for the flow.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>CI / validator</strong> — <code>validator/cli.py</code> enforces
        cross-node invariants and is the gate between human-reviewed YAML and the
        canonical corpus. Every change passes through it.
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-10 max-w-3xl">
    <h2>Current corpus (v{graph.kgVersion})</h2>
    <div class="mt-2 grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-5 gap-3">
      <div class="card"><div class="text-2xl font-sans font-semibold">{c.tools}</div><div class="text-sm text-ink-muted font-sans">Tools</div></div>
      <div class="card"><div class="text-2xl font-sans font-semibold">{c.failure_modes}</div><div class="text-sm text-ink-muted font-sans">Failure modes</div></div>
      <div class="card"><div class="text-2xl font-sans font-semibold">{c.taxonomies}</div><div class="text-sm text-ink-muted font-sans">Taxonomies</div></div>
      <div class="card"><div class="text-2xl font-sans font-semibold">{c.papers}</div><div class="text-sm text-ink-muted font-sans">Papers</div></div>
      <div class="card"><div class="text-2xl font-sans font-semibold">{c.crosswalks}</div><div class="text-sm text-ink-muted font-sans">Crosswalk edges</div></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-10 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2 max-w-3xl">
    <div class="card">
      <h3 class="!mt-0">Project</h3>
      <ul class="mt-2 list-disc pl-5 text-sm">
        <li><a href="https://github.com/saica-kg/saica-kg" rel="noopener">GitHub repository</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://github.com/saica-kg/saica-kg/blob/main/EDITORIAL_POLICY.md" rel="noopener">Editorial policy</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://github.com/saica-kg/saica-kg/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md" rel="noopener">Contributing</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://github.com/saica-kg/saica-kg/blob/main/LICENSE" rel="noopener">License (code: Apache-2.0)</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://github.com/saica-kg/saica-kg/blob/main/LICENSE-DATA" rel="noopener">License (data: CC-BY-4.0)</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3 class="!mt-0">Machine-readable</h3>
      <ul class="mt-2 list-disc pl-5 text-sm">
        <li><a href="/api/v1/snapshot.json"><code>/api/v1/snapshot.json</code></a> — full graph</li>
        <li><a href="/api/v1/tools.json"><code>/api/v1/tools.json</code></a></li>
        <li><a href="/api/v1/failure_modes.json"><code>/api/v1/failure_modes.json</code></a></li>
        <li><a href="/api/v1/taxonomies.json"><code>/api/v1/taxonomies.json</code></a></li>
        <li><a href="/api/v1/papers.json"><code>/api/v1/papers.json</code></a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-10 max-w-3xl">
    <h2>Citation</h2>
    <p>
      When citing SAICA-KG in user-facing output, use the phrase
      <em>"according to SAICA-KG (v{graph.kgVersion})"</em>. A full BibTeX block will ship
      with v0.1.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
